  "analysis": "Final round: control will repeat the proven 25/15/10 @ 0.3-0.7/same_class/uniform/0.15 (mAP 0.6116). Inclusion (AP 0.35) is the only weak class; round 2 showed 0.3-0.5 too small, prefer_small-all-classes hurt scratches, and 30/10/10 allocation hurt. So I keep the proven allocation and patches/scratches recipe, and test three single-factor inclusion nudges: (A) widen inclusion scale to 0.3-0.8 to cover mid-size misses (mid-tertile recall only 0.50); (B) scope prefer_small to inclusion only, since round 2 showed it lifted inclusion AP (0.384 vs 0.352) while the damage was to scratches, which I now protect; (C) raise inclusion max_overlap to 0.30 to create clustered multi-blob pastes matching clustered missed inclusions (val imgs 6, 10, 15) - the uncertain alternative. If none beats control, keep control.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "Mid-size inclusions are under-covered (mid-tertile recall 0.50 vs high 0.80) and 0.3-0.5 was too small while 0.3-0.7 worked; widening inclusion scale to 0.3-0.8 adds mid-size pastes (~63-72px from ~90px sources) without touching the small end. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 > 0.36 and mAP50 >= 0.61 vs control; if inclusion drops, the upper end is irrelevant and 0.3-0.7 stands.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 15, "scratches": 10},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.8, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Round 2 showed prefer_small raised inclusion AP (0.384 vs 0.352) but the mAP loss came from scratches (0.622 vs 0.712); scoping prefer_small to inclusion only should capture the inclusion gain while protecting scratches. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 >= 0.38 and scratches AP50 >= 0.69; if inclusion does not rise, source-size selection is not the lever and I keep uniform.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 15, "scratches": 10},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Several missed inclusions are clustered multi-blob defects (val images 6, 10, 15 show multiple dark spots in one region); raising inclusion max_overlap from 0.15 to 0.30 lets pastes cluster into multi-blob shapes resembling them. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 and small-tertile recall rise vs control; if inclusion drops, overlap creates unrealistic blends and I keep 0.15.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 15, "scratches": 10},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.3, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    }
  ]
}

